---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import StructureNext from "../../components/StructureNext.astro";
import LessonIllustration from "../../components/LessonIllustration.astro";
import StructureKindTag from "../../components/StructureKindTag.astro";
import ComplexityBadge from "../../components/ComplexityBadge.astro";
import { structureComplexity } from "../../lib/learning-complexity";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Maps"
  description="Compare ways to store named values when people edit them at the same time."
  territory="Structures"
  sheetTitle="Maps"
>
  <article class="map-family">
    <header class="page-intro">
      <p class="territory-label">Structure family</p>
      <h1>Maps</h1>
      <p>
        The ranger gives each hiker a notebook with a line for the gate status
        and another for the stockpile count. When they write different answers
        or cross out a line, how do their notebooks agree? They also need to
        agree when two hikers make a folder with the same name.
      </p>
      <LessonIllustration id="structures-maps" />
    </header>

    <section aria-labelledby="shared-map-title">
      <header><div><StructureKindTag kind="DDS" /><ComplexityBadge complexity={structureComplexity("shared-map")} /><h2 id="shared-map-title">SharedMap</h2><p>Use one shared order to select a value for each name.</p></div><code>map_kernel</code></header>
      <div class="structure-body">
        <div>
          <p>
            Alice writes "Trail open" on the gate-status line. Bob writes
            "Trail closed" on his copy before he sees her note. The ranger
            numbers Bob's change last, so all three hikers use his answer on
            that line. Their bridge-status line is unchanged.
          </p>
          <h3>Best for</h3>
          <ul><li>Shared JSON settings managed by one service</li><li>Named lines where the ranger can number every change</li></ul>
        </div>
        <dl><div><dt>Values</dt><dd>JSON and supported handles</dd></div><div><dt>When answers differ</dt><dd>Use the last numbered change for each line</dd></div><div><dt>Removal</dt><dd>Cross out one line or clear the notebook</dd></div></dl>
      </div>
      <a class="structure-link" href="/structures/shared-map/">Open the SharedMap lesson</a>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="lww-map-title">
      <header><div><StructureKindTag kind="CRDT" /><ComplexityBadge complexity={structureComplexity("lww-map")} /><h2 id="lww-map-title">LWWMap</h2><p>Compare the times beside each line to select a value.</p></div><code>lww_map_kernel</code></header>
      <div class="structure-body">
        <div>
          <p>
            Each hiker dates the change beside a named line. They use the
            latest date for that line, even if an older note arrives later.
            They keep the date and writer's name with the answer or crossed-out line.
          </p>
          <h3>Best for</h3>
          <ul><li>Offline text settings that need one predictable winner</li><li>Maps where clocks, not delivery order, define "last"</li></ul>
        </div>
        <dl><div><dt>Values</dt><dd>Text</dd></div><div><dt>When answers differ</dt><dd>Later time; if tied, crossed-out line, then writer</dd></div><div><dt>Removal</dt><dd>Keep the crossed-out line and its time</dd></div></dl>
      </div>
      <a class="structure-link" href="/structures/lww-map/">Open the LWWMap lesson</a>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="or-map-title">
      <header><div><StructureKindTag kind="CRDT" /><ComplexityBadge complexity={structureComplexity("or-map")} /><h2 id="or-map-title">OR-map</h2><p>New work can survive a removal made at the same time.</p></div><code>or_map_kernel</code></header>
      <div class="structure-body">
        <div>
          <p>
            Alice crosses out the Eagle Creek stockpile line after she sees
            5 crates. Bob records 3 more before he sees her change. When they
            compare notebooks, they keep the line and count all 8 crates
            because Bob added a new note.
          </p>
          <h3>Best for</h3>
          <ul><li>Named tallies and lists that combine new notes</li><li>Records where new work must survive a crossed-out line</li></ul>
        </div>
        <dl><div><dt>Values</dt><dd>Tallies, answers, or lists of names</dd></div><div><dt>When answers differ</dt><dd>Keep new notes the other hiker has not seen</dd></div><div><dt>Removal</dt><dd>Cross out only the notes already seen</dd></div></dl>
      </div>
      <a class="structure-link" href="/structures/or-map/">Open the OR-map lesson</a>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="directory-title">
      <header><div><StructureKindTag kind="DDS" /><ComplexityBadge complexity={structureComplexity("shared-directory")} /><h2 id="directory-title">SharedDirectory</h2><p>Track each folder separately when a name is reused.</p></div><code>directory_kernel</code></header>
      <div class="structure-body">
        <div>
          <p>
            Alice and Bob both make an Eagle Creek folder. The ranger treats
            them as one shared folder. If someone later removes it and makes
            another with the same name, old notes stay with the old folder.
          </p>
          <h3>Best for</h3>
          <ul><li>Shared project and document folders</li><li>Folder trees where names can be reused</li></ul>
        </div>
        <dl><div><dt>Values</dt><dd>Folders and named entries</dd></div><div><dt>When answers differ</dt><dd>Use shared order and track each folder separately</dd></div><div><dt>Removal</dt><dd>Delete one specific folder</dd></div></dl>
      </div>
      <a class="structure-link" href="/structures/shared-directory/">Open the SharedDirectory lesson</a>
    </section>

    <section class="family-comparison" aria-labelledby="map-choice-title">
      <h2 id="map-choice-title">Choose what happens when answers differ</h2>
      <table aria-label="Map comparison">
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Need</th><th scope="col">Choose</th><th scope="col">Main cost</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><th scope="row">One service orders JSON changes</th><td>SharedMap</td><td>The service must stay available</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Use clock times to select text values</th><td>LWWMap</td><td>Remember clocks and removals</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">New work survives removal</th><td>OR-map</td><td>Remember which work each person saw</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Folders can reuse names</th><td>SharedDirectory</td><td>Track each folder separately</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </section>

    <StructureNext />
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .map-family { max-width: var(--measure-reading); margin-inline: auto; }
  .page-intro { margin-bottom: var(--space-7); }
  .page-intro > p:last-of-type { font-size: 1.2rem; }
  .map-family > section:not(.family-comparison) {
    margin-top: var(--space-7);
    padding: var(--space-5);
    border: var(--rule-width) solid var(--line);
    background: var(--clear);
  }
  section > header {
    display: flex;
    align-items: start;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: var(--space-5);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-4);
    border-bottom: var(--rule-width) solid var(--line);
  }
  section h2, section header p { margin: 0; }
  section h2 { margin-block: var(--space-1); }
  section header code { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.8rem; white-space: nowrap; }
  .structure-body {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.3fr) minmax(15rem, 0.7fr);
    gap: var(--space-6);
    padding-block: var(--space-5);
  }
  .structure-body :is(p, h3) { margin-top: 0; }
  .structure-body h3 { margin-bottom: var(--space-2); font-size: 1rem; }
  dl { margin: 0; border-block: var(--rule-width) solid var(--line); }
  dl div { padding-block: var(--space-3); }
  dl div + div { border-top: var(--rule-width) solid var(--line-faint); }
  dt { color: var(--muted); font: 700 0.8rem/1.3 var(--font-ui); }
  dd { margin: var(--space-1) 0 0; }
  .structure-link { font-family: var(--font-ui); font-weight: 700; }
  .family-comparison { margin-top: var(--space-7); }
  table { width: 100%; margin-block: var(--space-4); border-collapse: collapse; }
  :is(th, td) { padding: var(--space-3); border-block: var(--rule-width) solid var(--line); text-align: left; vertical-align: top; }
  th { font-family: var(--font-ui); }
  @media (width < 48rem) {
    section > header, .structure-body { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    section > header { display: grid; }
  }
</style>
